CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: L0 artifact looks reproducible for the tested default: source-verified defaults, cross-process Go/Rust controls, and clock controls are adequate. Realistic workload is not yet established: packet lacks prevalence data showing production wazero hosts instantiate untrusted/security-sensitive WASI guests with bare NewModuleConfig(), and downstream prior art shows at least some hosts already know to pass crypto/rand.Reader and sys clocks.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. This is above bare CWE-330 only if framed narrowly as an ABI-boundary demotion of guest-level secure APIs plus deadline distortion under wazero defaults. However, the mechanism is not cleanly un-owned: wazero documents deterministic RandSource and fake clocks per knob, CrowdSec PR 4495 independently patches a real wazero embedding because the default “would defeat” randomness, and wetware/pkg issue 106 independently identifies guest crypto-grade entropy as a wazero WithRandSource concern. I do not find a retrieved source that owns the full cross-language crypto/rand/getrandom composition plus clock deadline artifact, so RED is too strong. GREEN is also too strong because the systems contribution is mostly a composed failure demonstration around documented defaults, and realistic-scale prevalence/security blast radius remains insufficient evidence.
